Template: homelab-invite/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host to bootstrap this app's roles/schema on:
 Used only once, at first install, to run homelab-bootstrap-app-role.

Template: homelab-invite/pgbouncer_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PgBouncer host to register this app's runtime role with:
 Used only once, at first install. Also written into config.yml's
 database.host, so the running service connects through the pooler.

Template: homelab-invite/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's homelab_api.base_url -- every gateway-routed
 request this app handles is authenticated by introspecting the
 caller's JWT here, and the public /invite/:token/accept page calls
 this same address's /api/v1/auth/register to actually create the
 account.

Template: homelab-invite/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 2514
Description: Port for homelab-invite to listen on:

Template: homelab-invite/advertise_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: This host's own address to advertise in the service registry:
 Written into config.yml's registry.host -- what homelab-api's gateway
 actually connects to when forwarding /api/v1/invites/* requests here,
 and what homelab-api's own _register handler dials directly for the
 /internal/v1/invites/consume call. Leave as 127.0.0.1 only if this
 service runs on the SAME host as homelab-api itself; set it to this
 host's real reachable address for any distributed deployment.

Template: homelab-invite/public_base_url
Type: string
Default: https://invite.test.mailmasker.org
Description: Public URL where the invite acceptance page is reachable:
 Written into every invite email's link -- must match whatever
 homelab-webproxy's sites.yml actually fronts this service as (see
 README.md's "Deployment" section). This is a completely different
 address from api_base above: that one is homelab-api's internal
 gateway, this one is the public page an invitee actually clicks.

Template: homelab-invite/account_domain
Type: string
Default:
Description: Fleet mail domain new invite-accepted logins are created under:
 When someone accepts an invite they choose a username, and their new
 account login becomes <username>@<this-domain>. Leave BLANK to derive
 it automatically from the mailer email's own domain below
 (invites@test.mailmasker.org -> test.mailmasker.org), which is the
 right answer on a normal single-domain install. Set it explicitly only
 if new accounts should live on a different fleet domain than the one
 the invite-sender mailbox is on.

Template: homelab-invite/invite_ttl_days
Type: string
Default: 14
Description: Days an invite link stays valid before it expires:

Template: homelab-invite/default_max_pending
Type: string
Default: 10
Description: Default max simultaneously-pending invites per sender:
 Per-sender overrides can be set later via `homelab-cli invite quota
 set` (site_admin only).

Template: homelab-invite/default_max_per_day
Type: string
Default: 5
Description: Default max invites a sender can send per rolling 24 hours:

Template: homelab-invite/mailer_email
Type: string
Default: invites@test.mailmasker.org
Description: System mailbox identity this service sends mail as:
 Must be a real, already-created account -- see `homelab-cli admin
 users create-service-account --email <this address>` (run this BEFORE
 finishing this install, or leave mailer_smtp_password blank and set it
 later with dpkg-reconfigure). See README.md's "Email sending" section
 for why this can't be an unauthenticated local relay.

Template: homelab-invite/mailer_smtp_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: SMTP submission host for the mailer identity above:
 127.0.0.1 only if homelab-postfix runs on this same host; otherwise
 that host's real reachable address.

Template: homelab-invite/mailer_smtp_port
Type: string
Default: 587
Description: SMTP submission port for the mailer identity above:

Template: homelab-invite/mailer_smtp_password
Type: password
Description: Password for the mailer identity above (blank = fill in later):
 The plaintext password `homelab-cli admin users create-service-account`
 printed once. Leave blank to finish this install anyway (outbound
 invite/welcome mail will fail until this is set) and paste it in later
 with dpkg-reconfigure homelab-invite.
